  "conclusions": [
    "Two credential-free POSTs to the observed StopsArrivals endpoint returned HTTP 401 with empty bodies.",
    "The second body was constructed and round-trip checked against the installed app request DTO: stopIds list and all default arrival-configuration fields, with optional time fields omitted.",
    "This demonstrates rejection of these anonymous requests; it does not isolate which header is required or establish the behavior of every Moovit endpoint.",
    "The normal app first launch called UserAuth/CreateUser with an API_KEY and without USER_KEY, receiving HTTP 200; later arrival requests carried API_KEY and USER_KEY without interactive Le Pass sign-in. This supports automatic guest credential setup.",
    "RTA public stop predictions returned HTTP 200 and XML without credentials. The late-evening response contained a cancelled scheduled departure, not a new live-vehicle prediction.",
    "No app credential values, cookies, account response values or access tokens were retained or replayed; the credential-free check did not call CreateUser."
  ],
